fact WorkItem(id: "WI-240", description: some(value: "Strategic: replace the dispatch-resolution fallback with a load-time-built sort_ops_table per operation-call-model.md §'Putting it together: dispatch end-to-end' ('sort symbols carry their own operations table … direct table lookup, not string concatenation + name resolution'). Today resolve_at_goal (anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs ~2670) and the apply_within eval dispatch step use `format!(\"{impl_qn}.{op_short}\").or_else(|| ... spec_qn ...)` — a try-impl-then-spec fallback that conflates two semantic cases (impl-overridden op vs spec-default rewrite-rule op) under one try/catch with string concatenation. This is the WI-237 feedback's reproducer: 'Ordered.lt — derived op (compare is primary); collect_provides_candidates finds the impl but resolve_at_goal's try_resolve_symbol(impl.lt).or(spec.lt) returns NoMatch'. Manifests today as the cmd_add_test + wi203_store_test bundle's stderr line 'WI-210 dispatch failed: no impl of anthill.prelude.Ordered.lt for the per-call bindings'. Strategic shape: introduce SortOpsTable { by_sort: HashMap<Symbol, HashMap<Symbol, Symbol>> } on KnowledgeBase, populated at load time once impl-side facts are asserted. For each impl sort S with `fact Spec[bindings]`, walk Spec's declared operations; for each op_short: if S declares op_short with a runnable body, entry = S.op_short; else if Spec declares op_short (rewrite-rule default), entry = Spec.op_short; else hard load error ('impl S missing op_short; spec has no default'). Dispatch consumers (typer's resolve_at_goal final lookup, eval's apply_within sort_ops_table[dict.sort][op_short]) collapse to a single kb.sort_ops_lookup(impl, op_short) — no string concatenation, no fallback. The default-method-inheritance rule moves from a try/catch at the call site to load-time data in the table; failure modes become precise and surfacing at load instead of dispatch. Estimated 200-300 LOC. NOTE: WI-240 fixes only the typer's Ordered.lt eprintln. The bundle's runtime crash 'var_ref(__req_main) unbound in requirement position' is a SEPARATE bug (typer drops current_occ during nested-apply arg descent in check_apply, leaving the inner call unclassified — tracked separately in WI-241). Both must land for cmd_add_test + wi203_store_test to pass. Acceptance: bundle Ordered.lt dispatch succeeds; the `.or_else(spec)` fallback in typing.rs is removed; eval's apply_within uses the table; cargo test green for anthill-core (bundle tests gated on WI-241 too)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-237"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-20T04:57:24Z"))
